# Example cron configuration for LG TV Price Monitor
# 
# To use this, run: crontab -e
# Then add one of the following lines (uncomment and adjust path):

# Check every 6 hours
# 0 */6 * * * cd /path/to/realmsofsilver-dvds && python3 scripts/monitor_tv_prices.py >> /tmp/tv_monitor.log 2>&1

# Check twice daily at 8 AM and 8 PM
# 0 8,20 * * * cd /path/to/realmsofsilver-dvds && python3 scripts/monitor_tv_prices.py >> /tmp/tv_monitor.log 2>&1

# Check once daily at 9 AM
# 0 9 * * * cd /path/to/realmsofsilver-dvds && python3 scripts/monitor_tv_prices.py >> /tmp/tv_monitor.log 2>&1

# Check every 4 hours
# 0 */4 * * * cd /path/to/realmsofsilver-dvds && python3 scripts/monitor_tv_prices.py >> /tmp/tv_monitor.log 2>&1

# Notes:
# - Replace /path/to/realmsofsilver-dvds with your actual repository path
# - Make sure Python 3 is installed: python3 --version
# - Install dependencies: pip3 install -r scripts/requirements.txt
# - Test first: python3 scripts/monitor_tv_prices.py --dry-run
# - Logs are written to /tmp/tv_monitor.log (or customize the path)
